<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zeus Polieus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> Polieus, Zeus of the city, was a form of the Greek god Zeus worshipped as protector of a city and its citizens. His cult was often shared with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena-polias">Athena Polias</a> on the acropolis, as at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, where the Dipolieia festival honoured him. Greek cities and colonies across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> delta, kept sanctuaries to him.</p></div>
